    "description": "Bluepoint Wind is an offshore wind development project planned in federal waters serving the New York and New Jersey markets. The project is intended to supply utility-scale renewable power into state-led offshore wind procurement programs and related power markets. Its operating model is asset-heavy and development-led, with value creation tied to permitting, interconnection, construction, and long-term contracted offtake rather than merchant-only exposure. Public project materials state that the lease area is located about 38 nautical miles off New York and 53 nautical miles off New Jersey and is designed for up to 2.4 GW of generation capacity. The project is owned by a partnership between Ocean Winds and Global Infrastructure Partners. The Bluepoint Wind name and public project branding were introduced in 2022 as the sponsors advanced the project in the Northeast U.S. offshore wind market.",
